-> [!CAUTION]
-> From 2027, Google wants Android phones to install only apps from developers registered with it, even outside the Play Store. **[Keep Android Open](https://keepandroidopen.org/)**
+# Tamaa Music — Android music app prototype
 
-<div align="center">
+A dark, Apple Music inspired Android client with a floating liquid glass dock and a YouTube Music catalog. This is a modified fork of [InterTune](https://github.com/ItzSkyeYT/InterTune), itself based on [OuterTune](https://github.com/OuterTune/OuterTune) and [InnerTune](https://github.com/z-huang/InnerTune). It is **not affiliated with Apple, YouTube, Google, or the upstream projects**. The original README is available in the pinned upstream Git history; upstream copyright notices and the GPL-3.0 license remain in place.
 
-<img src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ItzSkyeYT/InterTune/visionos-fix/assets/intertune.svg" width="140" height="140" alt="InterTune">
+## Design changes
 
-# InterTune
+- New app name, application ID (`id.tamaa.music`), and original music-note launcher icon.
+- Default charcoal theme and rose-red accent, with an editorial Listen Now heading and cleaner section headings.
+- A floating glass navigation dock, glass mini player, and player controls enabled by default. The existing Backdrop implementation uses blur, lens refraction and chromatic aberration on supported devices; Android 13+ is required for the live shader. Battery Saver uses a still frosted surface.
+- Default tabs: Listen Now, Albums, Artists, Library. Search remains available from the top search control.
+- Upstream-only services stay disabled by the upstream signing-key guard. The bundled upstream services properties were removed.
 
-<sub>InnerTune ∩ OuterTune</sub>
+This is a source prototype. It has not been compiled or tested on a device in this workspace because the Android SDK and Gradle distribution are not available here. The unofficial YouTube Music integration depends on changing internal endpoints and may require upstream fixes over time.
 
-### YouTube Music and your own music, in one Android app
